      "text": "To find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by both 3 and 6, we need to understand that any number divisible by 6 is also divisible by 3. Therefore, we only need to find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6.\n\nFirst, we identify the greatest three-digit number, which is 999. We then check if 999 is divisible by 6. A number is divisible by 6 if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.\n\n1. Check divisibility by 2: A number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even. The last digit of 999 is 9, which is odd. Therefore, 999 is not divisible by 2.\n2. Check divisibility by 3: A number is divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3. The sum of the digits of 999 is \\(9 + 9 + 9 = 27\\). Since 27 is divisible by 3, 999 is divisible by 3.\n\nSince 999 is not divisible by 2, we need to check the next lower number, 996, to see if it is divisible by 6.\n\n1. Check divisibility by 2: The last digit of 996 is 6, which is even. Therefore, 996 is divisible by 2.\n2. Check divisibility by 3: The sum of the digits of 996 is \\(9 + 9 + 6 = 24\\). Since 24 is divisible by 3, 996 is divisible by 3.\n\nSince 996 is divisible by both 2 and 3, it is divisible by 6. Therefore, the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6 is \\(\\boxed{996}\\).",
