      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the greatest possible three-digit number that is divisible by both 3 and 6, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the relationship between divisibility by 3 and 6:**\n   - A number is divisible by 6 if and only if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.\n   - A number is divisible by 3 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 3.\n   - A number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even.\n\n2. **Find the greatest three-digit number:**\n   - The greatest three-digit number is 999.\n\n3. **Check divisibility by 6:**\n   - A number is divisible by 6 if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.\n   - The last digit of 999 is 9, which is not even. Therefore, 999 is not divisible by 2.\n   - Since 999 is not divisible by 2, it cannot be divisible by 6.\n\n4. **Find the greatest even three-digit number:**\n   - The greatest even three-digit number is 998.\n\n5. **Check if 998 is divisible by 3:**\n   - Sum of the digits of 998: \\(9 + 9 + 8 = 26\\).\n   - Since 26 is not divisible by 3 (as \\(26 \\div 3 \\approx 8.67\\)), 998 is not divisible by 3.\n\n6. **Find the greatest even three-digit number that is divisible by 3:**\n   - We need to find the largest even number less than or equal to 998.\n   - We start from 998 and subtract 1 each time until we find an even number:\n     \\[\n     998 - 1 = 997 \\quad (\\text{not even})\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     996 - 1 = 995 \\quad (\\text{not even})\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     994 - 1 = 993 \\quad (\\text{not even})\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     992 - 1 = 991 \\quad (\\text{not even})\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     990 - 1 = 989 \\quad (\\text{not even})\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     988 - 1 = 987 \\quad (\\text{even})\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, 987 is the greatest even three-digit number.\n\n7. **Check if 987 is divisible by 6:**\n   - Sum of the digits of 987: \\(9 + 8 + 7 = 24\\).\n   - Since 24 is divisible by 3, 987 is divisible by 3.\n   - Since 987 is even, it is also divisible by 2.\n\n8. **Conclusion:**\n   - 987 is the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by both 3 and 6.\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{987}\\).",
